Problem Statement: Write a Java program to create an abstract class with an abstract method and extend it in a subclass that provides an implementation.


abstract class Vehicle { 
abstract void start(); 


 void fuelType() { 
 System.out.println("Vehicle uses fuel."); 

 } 

} 

class Car extends Vehicle { 
	
	
void start() { 
System.out.println("Car starts with a key."); 
} 
} 


public class AbstractClassDemo { 
public static void main(String[] args) { 

	
Vehicle v = new Car(); 
v.start();       

v.fuelType();  
} 
} 
